# Build + run scratch (not source)
/dist/
/.rw-bin
*.log
# `go build ./...` drops one binary per cmd/* package at the module root, named
# after its directory — ./worker, ./guest-agent, ./microvm-worker, ./vmpoolctl (plus
# a .exe suffix on a GOOS=windows build). /worker's own entry predates this comment
# (it was ./remote-worker before the entrypoint moved to cmd/worker); the rest are
# added together so the six-way cross-platform `go build`/`go vet` check the P4
# microVM tasks run from this directory never leaves an untracked-and-unignored
# binary sitting next to go.mod again.
/worker
/remote-worker
/guest-agent
/guest-agent.exe
/microvm-worker
/microvm-worker.exe
/vmpoolctl
/vmpoolctl.exe
